# Local LangGraph runner

This editable TypeScript source belongs to the consumer. It stays outside runtime
configuration and has independent pinned dependencies and an npm lockfile. The
scaffold does not install packages, build images, start a cluster, or run the graph.

The finite graph performs two deterministic steps and reports a JSON outcome on
stdout. It requires EXPHERE_RUNTIME_ID and EXPHERE_RUN_ID; the runtime lifecycle
injects them into the Job. It contains no model calls, MCP connections, remote
memory, hosted telemetry, credentials, persistent state, or HTTP server. Unknown
financial cost is null; zero model calls does not prove zero infrastructure cost.
Failures go to stderr; termination signals request cancellation.

## Consumer build

Run `npm ci --ignore-scripts` and `npm run build` in this directory to inspect the
compiled source, or build the supplied Dockerfile with your chosen local image tag.
Image construction is a separate consumer action with network and resource costs.
The Dockerfile base tag is mutable: select a reviewed digest for reproducible builds.

Use `ex cluster load-image <your-image>` after explicitly creating the project
cluster. In guided runtime initialization select this directory as the component,
use its directory name as the unit name, choose Job, and supply the image and resource
requests/limits. A Job has no HTTP readiness path, service port, or replicas input.
Native Job files own deadline, retry, and parallelism settings. The generated defaults
are one completion, one worker, no retries, and a 120-second deadline.

Dependencies: LangGraph 1.5.0, LangChain Core 1.2.17, Zod 4.6.7, TypeScript 5.9.3,
and Node 22 types 22.19.11. Runtime target: Node 22. Read the upstream graph model at
https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langgraph/graph-api before extending it.
Generation and compilation do not demonstrate Kubernetes execution or cleanup.
